From b3ae470c6d4775c81f6066308a3f502f00df2a62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Bloomin <452472+daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:56:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): hermes kanban create and REST POST /tasks
 refuse a second owner too [daveey]

The create_overlap check (d0cc66e9f4) ran only in the kanban_create tool, so
the CLI and the dashboard/REST create endpoint could still create a duplicate
owner. Both now call kanban_overlap.check: CLI --distinct-from (repeatable) +
--distinct-reason, exit 2 with the refusal (JSON on stdout under --json); REST
distinct_from + distinct_reason, 409 with the refusal as detail. Idempotency
retries skip the check, and a keyed creator (coach/self-heal crons) is never
blocked by open cards of its own key family (text before the first ':').
Parity tests cover a refused duplicate and an accepted override per path.
